== (6) power and upper bound ==
  test-era residual-vs-market coefficient se = 0.480 pts/s -> a train-sized effect (-0.30) has power ~0.09; minimum detectable |effect| at 80% power ~1.34 pts/s
  market-free 2023-25 in-sample se = 0.516: the 2009-19 coefficient (-0.54) is 1.30 se from the 2023-25 estimate -> 'the effect vanished' is NOT statistically established, only 'not detected'
  realized game plays vs market residual (test): corr=+0.302; prior spp_avg -> realized plays R^2 = 0.014 (train 0.087)
  -> even perfect knowledge of realized plays explains 9.1% of market residual variance; prior pace predicts 1.4% of plays -> upper bound on pace's residual R^2 ~ 0.12%

